jobs.jd:
We are seeking a Senior Mechanical Engineer to join our Manufacturing team, with direct responsibility for the design, build and improvement of the tooling, fixtures and equipment that underpin our in-house manufacturing capability. Working closely with our Design, Assembly and Process teams, you will help bridge the gap between lab scale, pilot and high-volume manufacturing.
Role responsibilities
- Lead the team responsible for design and implementation of in-house tooling to support our efforts to scale manufacturing;
- Design, build and continuously improve in-house tooling, fixtures and equipment;
- Take new tooling and equipment from concept through CAD design, fabrication, build and commissioning on the factory floor;
- Provide hands-on support to the manufacturing team - troubleshooting, modifying and improving equipment;
- Collaborate with Design, Assembly and Process teams to implement new cell architectures and manufacturing processes;
- Meet design requirements through rapid, iterative prototyping;
- Work with Hysata partners and vendors to define, develop, validate and commission manufacturing tools and equipment;
- Define and execute validation plans;
- Develop SOPs and safety protocols for new tools, equipment and processes.
Key skills
- Engineering degree in Mechanical, Manufacturing or a similar field;
- Strong background in mechanical design engineering, with proven hands-on capability to build, modify and commission what you design;
- Proficiency in computer-aided design (NX preferred);
- Fabrication experience - hands-on R&D, design, build and test;
- Contributed to delivering complex projects requiring new tooling, equipment and process development, including equipment specification;
- Demonstrated experience with DFMA, DFMEA, validation testing, materials selection and process technology selection.
Valued skills
- 5+ years of experience in a similar tooling, equipment or mechanical design role;
- Experience introducing and optimising tooling and equipment in a manufacturing scale-up environment;
- PFMEA, QA/QC, SOP, design and process validation;
- Experience with electrolysers, battery or energy storage systems a plus.
